From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Alexander M. Merritt" <alexander@edera.dev>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:10:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hw/char/serial-pci: add options to set the PCI IDs

Linux's 8250_pci claims Graviton's console by its IDs, 1d0f:8250,
and reads BAR 0 whatever its type. It claims pci-serial only through
its guess for a UART of the communication class, which needs an I/O
BAR, so it leaves a pci-serial with a memory BAR alone, and nothing
in the guest touches the UART as it would on Graviton.

Let the user give the device other IDs.

Signed-off-by: Alexander M. Merritt <alexander@edera.dev>
---
 docs/specs/pci-serial.rst | 2 +-
 hw/char/serial-pci.c      | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docs/specs/pci-serial.rst b/docs/specs/pci-serial.rst
index f0bb70c905..6163f68a43 100644
--- a/docs/specs/pci-serial.rst
+++ b/docs/specs/pci-serial.rst
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ Single-port card
 Name:
   ``pci-serial``
 PCI ID:
-  1b36:0002
+  1b36:0002, or the IDs that ``x-vendor-id`` and ``x-device-id`` give
 PCI Region 0:
    IO bar, 8 bytes long, with the 16550 UART mapped to it. With
    ``x-memory-bar=on``, a memory bar of 4 KiB instead, with the UART at
diff --git a/hw/char/serial-pci.c b/hw/char/serial-pci.c
index 0f7f07934f..90018f2226 100644
--- a/hw/char/serial-pci.c
+++ b/hw/char/serial-pci.c
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ struct PCISerialState {
     SerialState state;
     bool memory_bar;
     MemoryRegion bar;
+    uint16_t vendor_id;
+    uint16_t device_id;
 };
 
 /* A memory BAR is one page, with the UART's registers at its start. */
@@ -74,6 +76,8 @@ static void serial_pci_realize(PCIDevice *dev, Error **errp)
         return;
     }
 
+    pci_set_word(pci->dev.config + PCI_VENDOR_ID, pci->vendor_id);
+    pci_set_word(pci->dev.config + PCI_DEVICE_ID, pci->device_id);
     pci->dev.config[PCI_CLASS_PROG] = 2; /* 16550 compatible */
     pci->dev.config[PCI_INTERRUPT_PIN] = 1;
     s->irq = pci_allocate_irq(&pci->dev);
@@ -112,6 +116,10 @@ static const VMStateDescription vmstate_pci_serial = {
 
 static const Property serial_pci_properties[] = {
     DEFINE_PROP_BOOL("x-memory-bar", PCISerialState, memory_bar, false),
+    DEFINE_PROP_UINT16("x-vendor-id", PCISerialState, vendor_id,
+                       PCI_VENDOR_ID_REDHAT),
+    DEFINE_PROP_UINT16("x-device-id", PCISerialState, device_id,
+                       PCI_DEVICE_ID_REDHAT_SERIAL),
 };
 
 static void serial_pci_class_initfn(ObjectClass *klass, const void *data)
